From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GDmio <zhalin66@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:53:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/32] BlueOS: SystemUI: Brand default color, palette for the
 boot animation

Until the user picks colors in Wallpaper & style the system palette comes from the BlueOS brand color (#128AFA, stored as a preset). The current palette is published to persist.bootanim.color1..4 so dynamically colored boot animations follow it.

Change-Id: Id3bd0b1b4fb7e6ac72836cac8717735ab35a67de
---
 .../theme/ThemeOverlayController.java         | 58 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 56 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/theme/ThemeOverlayController.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/theme/ThemeOverlayController.java
index ea7a1925d5ef..495df3297a3e 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/theme/ThemeOverlayController.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/theme/ThemeOverlayController.java
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@ import android.database.ContentObserver;
 import android.graphics.Color;
 import android.net.Uri;
 import android.os.Handler;
